            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0472" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5103: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-10-28T14:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">October 28,
                                1927—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>301. President Diaz has asked the information, if possible by December 1st,
                    regarding the chief points in the new electoral law to be proposed by General
                    McCoy in order that he may discuss the matter in his message at the opening of
                    Congress.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Munro</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
